   C                                    Non-target cetaceans, such as Dall's porpoise, were routinely reported using
   C                                    the "t" event that is normally used to record turtle sightings. There are no
   C                                    sighting forms or sighting numbers for these non-target cetacean sightings. These
   C                                    data were edited with the existing checks for turtle data except that the species
   C                                    codes checks were the same as for normal cetacean sightings (spcodes.dat). A.J. 1/14/05.
   C 
   C                                    The marine mammal sightings that were originally recorded in the "t" event records 
   C                                    were reformatted to the standard S-A-1 event sequence on 30 Apr 2010 by A. Jackson. 
   C                                    DasCheck was run on the revised file and the data edited.
   C 
   C                                    During the SPLASH cruise, there were frequent periods when fog reduced the
   C                                    search distance to less than one mile.  During those periods, observers
   C                                    typically were required to vacate the flying bridge to avoid being exposed
   C                                    to the fog horn.  Effort was maintained during these periods by an observer
   C                                    watch on the bridge deck.  Effort was sometimes reduced to one or two
   C                                    observers, depending on visible search area and the number of people required
   C                                    to adequately view this area.  To maintain comparability with definitions of
   C                                    search effort used during previous SWFSC surveys, users of these data may
   C                                    want to limit analyses to periods when three people are on watch and when
   C                                    visibility is one mile or greater. J. Barlow 2/15/05.
   C
